# Every ignore needs a reason and an owner. Review this file when you touch the code it covers.

# bootstrap: the apply role uses AdministratorAccess until the scoped policy is switched on (Post 18).
AWS-0057

# Public load balancer on purpose: plat-alb is the internet entry point of the lab API.
AWS-0053

# The lab allows all outbound traffic from application security groups.
AWS-0104

# bootstrap: the state bucket uses SSE-S3 (AES256). A customer-managed key would add a key to bootstrap before anything else exists, and every reader of state would need kms:Decrypt.
AWS-0132

# ECR repository allows mutable tags because the lab re-pushes :latest (Post 10). Production would set IMMUTABLE and push unique tags.
AWS-0031

# plat-alerts topic is unencrypted: CloudWatch alarms, EventBridge and Budgets cannot publish to a topic encrypted with the AWS-managed key. A customer-managed key plus policy grants would be needed (Post 14 explains the pitfall).
AWS-0095

# The lab Deployment runs stock nginx, which needs root and a writable filesystem. A real workload would set a non-root user and readOnlyRootFilesystem.
KSV-0014
KSV-0118
